cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this container, please cite it as below. It packages the FaMAF CVA6
  Project's additions on top of the OpenHW Group's CORE-V CVA6, which is cited
  under references along with its paper.
title: "FaMAF CVA6 Project: the CVA6 container"
abstract: >-
  A Docker image holding the frozen CORE-V CVA6 fork used as the real-hardware
  side of a thesis at FaMAF, Universidad Nacional de Córdoba, on how closely a
  gem5 MinorCPU configuration can be made to match a real RISC-V core. It ships
  the core with a built RISC-V toolchain, Verilator and Spike, the calibration
  benchmarks and the programs written while developing the viewer, the
  Verilator run drivers and both sweeps, the windowed waveform dump, and the
  CVA6Flow pipeline viewer.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Nieto"
    given-names: "Manuel"
    affiliation: "FaMAF, Universidad Nacional de Córdoba"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3893-5628"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/FaMAF-CVA6-Project/CVA6/blob/master/dockerfiles/CVA6/LICENSE.FaMAF"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FaMAF-CVA6-Project/CVA6"
url: "https://hub.docker.com/r/manuel313/famaf_cva6"
keywords:
  - RISC-V
  - CVA6
  - Verilator
  - RTL simulation
  - computer architecture
  - microarchitecture
  - simulator calibration
  - Docker
